endpoints.responseShape:
{
  "template": {
    "key": "cardiology",
    "label": "Cardiology Exam",
    "icon": "🫀",
    "sections": [
      { "title": "Cardiac Symptoms", "fields": [
          { "key": "chest_pain", "label": "Chest Pain", "type": "select", "options": ["None","Typical angina","Atypical angina","Nonanginal","Unspecified"] },
          { "key": "nyha_class", "label": "NYHA Class", "type": "select", "options": ["I","II","III","IV"] },
          { "key": "palpitations", "label": "Palpitations", "type": "select", "options": ["None","Intermittent","Persistent"] },
          { "key": "syncope", "label": "Syncope/Pre-syncope", "type": "select", "options": ["None","Pre-syncope","Syncope"] } ] },
      ...
    ]
  }
}

Exactly ONE top-level key, `template`, holding the identical object structure that GET /specialty-template returns in its `template` slot: {key, label, icon, sections:[{title, paired?, fields:[{key, label, type, placeholder?, unit?, options?}]}]}. `sections` and `fields` are always non-empty arrays for the 11 real keys. Field `type` is one of: text | number | select | date | textarea.

{
  "suggestedCodes": [
    { "code": "E11.9", "description": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus without complications", "confidence": 0.92 },
    { "code": "I10",   "description": "Essential (primary) hypertension",              "confidence": 0.81 }
  ],
  "aiProvider": "gemini" | "openai" | "micromind",
  "aiModel": "gemini-2.0-flash" | "gpt-4o" | "micromind-agent"
}

Exactly 3 top-level keys in this order. Each element of suggestedCodes has EXACTLY these 3 keys in this order: code, description, confidence — any extra keys the model emits are dropped by the .map().
`suggestedCodes` is ALWAYS AN ARRAY, never null, and is `[]` (not null, not absent) when the model output cannot be parsed, when every suggestion is filtered out, or when the array is empty. Max length 8.
`code` is uppercased and truncated to 10 chars; `description` truncated to 200 chars; `confidence` is a number clamped to [0,1], defaulting to 0.5 when the model omitted it or sent a non-number.
Nothing is written to the DB, so there is no id/visitId on the items — these are transient suggestions the client stages locally.
